From: LA32R bringup <bringup@local>
Subject: [PATCH] loongarch: dts: poll LA32R UART0 instead of using IRQ for A/B

Linux reaches userspace on the FPGA but ttyS0 input is corrupted or lost,
while the same UART works with uCore's polling input path.  Reducing the
16550A RX FIFO trigger to one byte did not fix the failure, so bypass the
external interrupt path entirely for the board UART at 0x1fe001e0.

The 8250 OF driver treats a missing interrupt as IRQ 0 and its universal
8250 layer then services the port with serial8250_timeout().  This is a
diagnostic/software-workaround build: success implicates UART IRQ generation,
clear/EOI, interrupt-controller routing, or CDC rather than the RBR data path.
---
 arch/loongarch/boot/dts/loongson/loongson32_ls.dts | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/loongarch/boot/dts/loongson/loongson32_ls.dts b/arch/loongarch/boot/dts/loongson/loongson32_ls.dts
--- a/arch/loongarch/boot/dts/loongson/loongson32_ls.dts
+++ b/arch/loongarch/boot/dts/loongson/loongson32_ls.dts
@@ -52,8 +52,6 @@
                         compatible = "ns16550a";
                         reg = < 0x1fe001e0  0x10>;
                         clock-frequency = <33000000>;
-                        interrupt-parent = <&cpuic>;
-                        interrupts = <2>;
                         no-loopback-test;
                 };

